  "id": "khap_thum_luang_prabang",
  "name": "Khap thum (Luang Prabang repartee song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Vocal genre of Luang Prabang, the former royal capital of northern Laos, in which male and female singers alternate verses of courtship and wit. Unlike the khaen-accompanied lam and khap of other regions, khap thum is accompanied by a classical ensemble of the Luang Prabang type, with xylophone, gong circle, fiddle, flute, drum and cymbals, which plays between the sung verses. It is documented in Lao National Radio recordings and in Terry Miller's research.",
  "recipe": "classic modern khap thum, art Music, southeast Asian branch. duet. ranat ek, khong wong yai, so u, lao ching chap open and damped ching, credited bamboo flute unspecified, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
